### Health Check / API Info
GET http://localhost:4000/paystack

### Initialize Payment
POST http://localhost:4000/paystack/initialize
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "amount": 3000,
  "currency": "KES",
  "metadata": {
    "custom_fields": [
      {
        "display_name": "Customer Name",
        "variable_name": "customer_name",
        "value": "John Doe"
      }
    ]
  }
}

### Verify Payment (Replace REFERENCE with actual reference from initialize response)
POST http://localhost:4000/paystack/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reference": "tl3dk4bo65"
}

### Test Verify Payment with Invalid Reference
POST http://localhost:4000/paystack/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reference": "invalid_reference_12345"
}

### Test Initialize Payment - Missing Email
POST http://localhost:4000/paystack/initialize
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 3000
}

### Test Initialize Payment - Missing Amount
POST http://localhost:4000/paystack/initialize
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@example.com"
}

### Get Payment by Reference
GET http://localhost:4000/paystack/payment/tl3dk4bo65

### Get All Payments (with pagination)
GET http://localhost:4000/paystack/payments?limit=10&offset=0

### Get All Payments - Default (50 items)
GET http://localhost:4000/paystack/payments

### Test Initialize Payment - Invalid Email Format
POST http://localhost:4000/paystack/initialize
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "amount": 3000
}

### Test Initialize Payment - Invalid Amount (negative)
POST http://localhost:4000/paystack/initialize
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "amount": -100
}

### Test Initialize Payment - Invalid Amount (zero)
POST http://localhost:4000/paystack/initialize
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "amount": 0
}

### Webhook Test (Paystack will send POST requests here)
POST http://localhost:4000/webhook/paystack
Content-Type: application/json
x-paystack-signature: test_signature

{
  "event": "charge.success",
  "data": {
    "reference": "test_reference",
    "amount": 300000,
    "currency": "KES",
    "status": "success"
  }
}